  "notes": "List prices from the aquafunded.com homepage pricing widget (every market/model/type/size clicked, 2026-10-31); fees shown are pre-discount list prices. Promo on own site today: code HALLOWEEN = 35% off (\"Halloween Sale 35% OFF + 200% Refund\", \"Limited Time\", no expiry date stated); widget also shows multi-account discounts (2nd account -40%, 3rd -45%). Homepage says fees are \"100% refundable\"; help centre/refund policy: evaluation fee refunded with the 4th payout, not refunded if hard-breached before then. Futures Flex is sold in two variants (no daily loss limit vs a $ daily loss limit; DLL amount not captured); futures accounts use EOD drawdown and position caps (4 contracts/40 micros; Instant 1 contract/10 micros); futures payouts capped per cycle (e.g. Standard 50K $2,000 then $2,500). Futures models list no minimum trading days on the widget, so programs show null. Help centre also documents Pay After Pass ($5 evaluation + activation fee after passing), TryAqua $1/$10 and legacy models (1 Step Pro, 3 Step, AquaMan); these are not in the homepage pricing widget today and are not listed as programs. Headline rule fields describe 2 Step Standard. min_trading_days=3 (1 Step/2 Step Standard/Elite; each day needs >=0.5% profit); Instant models need 5 (Flex 7) qualifying days before a reward. News: allowed but profit from trades opened/closed within 5 min of red-folder/FOMC events is capped at 0.5% of starting balance per payout cycle (accounts from 27 Apr 2026). Other funded-account rules: max floating loss per trade (Instant Standard 1%, Pro 2%; three-strike split cuts), WaveStop on some models, 80% margin-usage cap, trades under 2 minutes may be treated as tick scalping (profit removal). Payouts: $100 minimum, 3% processing fee on all payouts, first two rewards capped at $10,000 each on $100K+ accounts. Restricted list above is full ban; Thailand, Brazil, Bulgaria, Japan, Jordan, Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia, Philippines are limited to Instant 